Imports:
  - Types:
      - EntityContract
      - RoutineContract
    Usages:
      - contract_data
    From: goga/contract/data

Usages:
  conventions: .goga/usages/conventions.md
  tree-sitter-js: .goga/usages/cooks/tree-sitter-js.md

Annotations: |
  During development and testing, use the practice `conventions`.
  For parsing JavaScript files, use the practice `tree-sitter-js`.

---

"javascript_contract(cell_path: str) -> contracts:list[EntityContract | RoutineContract]":
  location: javascript.py
  annotations: |
    Collect all exported objects from the JavaScript module facade at the specified path.
    Use the practice `contract_data` to form the results.

    `cell_path`: path to the JavaScript module (directory with index.js)

    Algorithm:
    - find index.js in the specified directory
    - parse AST via the practice `tree-sitter-js` (JavaScript grammar)
    - extract exported declarations:
      - ESM: export function, export class, export { ... }, export default
      - CommonJS: module.exports = { ... }, module.exports = functionName
    - for class → EntityContract: fields → properties, methods → methods
    - for function → RoutineContract
    - types are extracted from JSDoc comments (@param, @returns, @type)

    Requirements:
    - only exported declarations are included in the contract
    - types from JSDoc are included in the contract
    - argument order matters
    - camelCase for function/method names, PascalCase for classes
    - when JSDoc annotations are absent, the signature type is an empty string
    - for class properties, the signature is the return type from JSDoc @type, or an empty string
    - EntityContract for class gets signature="()": instance creation via new

